{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"Fastfetch-cli.Fastfetch","latestVersion":"2.71.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Like neofetch, but much faster because written mostly in C.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Like neofetch, but much faster because written mostly in C.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","name":"fastfetch","packageUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch","publisher":"fastfetch-cli","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli","releaseNotes":"Features:\n- Added a spin logo type (--logo-type spin), which animates the built-in logo or a text file as a 3D slab that rotates. (Logo)\n- This logo type requires --watch <s>/--dynamic-interval <ms> being set to enable animation. For example: fastfetch --logo-type spin --watch 1 will animate the logo every second.\n- --logo-spin-speed-per-frame sets the degrees per drawn frame (default 10); --logo-spin-speed-per-round sets the seconds one revolution takes and wins when both are given. Both accept a negative value to turn the other way.\n- --logo-spin-angle picks the frame to start from, and is the only frame drawn without --watch.\n- Optimised display detection on GNOME and Cinnamon Wayland sessions. (Display, Linux)\n\nBugfixes:\n- Don’t detect mise and atuin as shells. (#2686, Shell)\n- Rejected an empty separator.string in the JSON config with an error message. (#2689, Separator)\n- Fixed fastfetch blocking forever when the terminal answered a terminal query only partially, for example with just one of the two OSC 10/11 color replies. (Logo / Terminal / TerminalTheme, Unix / Windows)\n- Fixed a $ ending a logo line or the logo itself being parsed as the start of a color code instead of a plain dollar sign. (#2666, Logo)\n- Fixed AMD GPU name detection in amdgpu.ids when PCI device ID or revision ID has leading zeros. (GPU, Linux)\n- Improved uptime detection on SunOS via kstat. (#2674, Uptime, SunOS)\n- Fixed substring formatting returning the remaining string when a negative end index is before the start of the string. (General)\n- Fixed a skipped {?} / {/} conditional in a format string ending at the {?} / {/} of a conditional nested in it. (General)\n- Fixed numbers in format strings that don’t fit in 32 bits wrapping around to a valid argument index, constant index, substring index or length, e.g. {4294967297} being read as {1}, and a signed integer overflow for {1:-2147483648}. (General)\n- Fixed substring formatting printing the placeholder as is, instead of nothing, when the start index is outside of the string and an end index is given. (General)\n- Fixed the CPU micro-architecture level (march) being under-reported on Windows on ARM when IsProcessorFeaturePresent does not expose a feature the CPU implements. (CPU, Windows)\n- It is now decoded from the AArch64 ID registers in the registry, matching the Linux detection.\n\nLogos:\n- Added Tiny Core Linux (#2655)\n- Added ArmadaOS (#2649)\n- Added AstrOS (#2582)\n- Added openSUSE Leap Micro (#2703)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/releases/tag/2.71.0","tags":["cli","command-line","cross-platform","fastfetch","fetch","hardware","neofetch","screenfetch","terminal"]}},"name":"fastfetch","packageUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch","publisher":"fastfetch-cli","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli","releaseNotes":"Features:\n- Added a spin logo type (--logo-type spin), which animates the built-in logo or a text file as a 3D slab that rotates. (Logo)\n- This logo type requires --watch <s>/--dynamic-interval <ms> being set to enable animation. For example: fastfetch --logo-type spin --watch 1 will animate the logo every second.\n- --logo-spin-speed-per-frame sets the degrees per drawn frame (default 10); --logo-spin-speed-per-round sets the seconds one revolution takes and wins when both are given. Both accept a negative value to turn the other way.\n- --logo-spin-angle picks the frame to start from, and is the only frame drawn without --watch.\n- Optimised display detection on GNOME and Cinnamon Wayland sessions. (Display, Linux)\n\nBugfixes:\n- Don’t detect mise and atuin as shells. (#2686, Shell)\n- Rejected an empty separator.string in the JSON config with an error message. (#2689, Separator)\n- Fixed fastfetch blocking forever when the terminal answered a terminal query only partially, for example with just one of the two OSC 10/11 color replies. (Logo / Terminal / TerminalTheme, Unix / Windows)\n- Fixed a $ ending a logo line or the logo itself being parsed as the start of a color code instead of a plain dollar sign. (#2666, Logo)\n- Fixed AMD GPU name detection in amdgpu.ids when PCI device ID or revision ID has leading zeros. (GPU, Linux)\n- Improved uptime detection on SunOS via kstat. (#2674, Uptime, SunOS)\n- Fixed substring formatting returning the remaining string when a negative end index is before the start of the string. (General)\n- Fixed a skipped {?} / {/} conditional in a format string ending at the {?} / {/} of a conditional nested in it. (General)\n- Fixed numbers in format strings that don’t fit in 32 bits wrapping around to a valid argument index, constant index, substring index or length, e.g. {4294967297} being read as {1}, and a signed integer overflow for {1:-2147483648}. (General)\n- Fixed substring formatting printing the placeholder as is, instead of nothing, when the start index is outside of the string and an end index is given. (General)\n- Fixed the CPU micro-architecture level (march) being under-reported on Windows on ARM when IsProcessorFeaturePresent does not expose a feature the CPU implements. (CPU, Windows)\n- It is now decoded from the AArch64 ID registers in the registry, matching the Linux detection.\n\nLogos:\n- Added Tiny Core Linux (#2655)\n- Added ArmadaOS (#2649)\n- Added AstrOS (#2582)\n- Added openSUSE Leap Micro (#2703)","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/releases/tag/2.71.0","tags":["cli","command-line","cross-platform","fastfetch","fetch","hardware","neofetch","screenfetch","terminal"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.71.0/app.json","detailSha256":"b0c63ecf7c8ad111bca0543d11190b73ad0ab249b756c48daa84b46fa8c37e04","releaseDate":"2026-11-06","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"2.71.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.70.0/app.json","detailSha256":"8d2ced62412ce857f1d525e5136937244fc99816992707865c12286c6a7cc415","releaseDate":"2026-10-14","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.70.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.69.0/app.json","detailSha256":"ff3d159ca287402efc034dfbd2ba7893a8e94bfdf2f05df3b68ffcb3c9aeeac5","releaseDate":"2026-09-25","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.69.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.68.1/app.json","detailSha256":"0358c4ab37a74bc5c40679bd07550a500300bfc190f64b4c9937dc2835ebad45","releaseDate":"2026-09-01","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.68.1"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.68.0/app.json","detailSha256":"6ab2d6907110cc6062ffc9c9c3ebe9c86e4e44da386031ff2ad4119bbfc6dc55","releaseDate":"2026-09-01","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.68.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.67.1/app.json","detailSha256":"8e8fdfcbc4f19ca46a6d33499f8a4b1f80d9ae2499be44a1dea46fcce0a1b8c0","releaseDate":"2026-08-14","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.67.1"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64"],"detailPath":"versions/2.67.0/app.json","detailSha256":"6d90a21a538db492b3a142219832